# Building

This is where you actually make your project.

You can build almost anything.

## Software

Websites, apps, games, bots, AI tools, and more.

Useful tools:

- VS Code
- GitHub
- Hackatime

## Hardware

PCBs, electronics, robotics, 3D printing, and physical projects.

Useful tools:

- CAD software
- PCB design tools
- Hardware guides

## Tracking your time

Your build time is tracked through Hackatime.

Every hour of shipped work earns you **50 pixels**.

---

# Shipping

Building something is only half the journey.

Shipping means submitting your project for review.

The flow is:

1. Build your project
2. Write up what you made
3. Submit it for review
4. Get approved
5. Receive your pixels and rewards

Before submitting, check what makes a good submission. Reviewers want to see what you built, what you learned, and what makes your project yours.

---

# Rewards

Pixels are your currency in Pixl.

You earn them by shipping projects.

## Earning pixels

- **50 pixels per hour** of shipped work
- Extra prizes from certain sidequests

## Spending pixels

Pixels can be spent in the shop.

Rewards can include:

- Stickers
- Hardware
- Other builder gear
- Bigger prizes like a MacBook Air

Keep building, keep shipping, and keep unlocking more.

---

# Free stuff to help you build

You shouldn't have to spend your own money to start building.

Hack Club provides:

- Free AI credits for building your own agents and tools. Not for just running a pre-built coding assistant.
- Free hosting on Nest, a Linux server you can put basically anything on.
- Free domains — open a PR on the DNS repo and claim one.
- Free CDN for images, video, and other assets.

